Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D1: CPU per draw: cs_flush_load_to() checks pending loads with one 64-bit test instead of looping the 256-bit bitset per operand (ALWAYS_INLINE), and cs_alloc_ins_block() gets an inline fast path with the chunk-linking slow path out of line (.text -0.94 MB); command stream bit-identical, no switch
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/022
Validation test: host csdiff: 20,000 random CS sequences (68,069,136 instructions, chunk linking, alloc failures) byte-identical old vs new, mutation check fails on sequence 0; host timing 49-55 -> 26 ns per 14-instruction draw sequence; draw-path batch rg477m/023-027 on the device (drawcpu bench, DXVK pattern, 20,000 draws x 20 reps, pinned A715 at max clock, 10 interleaved runs per build): 543.6 -> 467.9 ns per recorded draw (-14%), with rg477m/024-027 switched off 501.8 (this patch about -8%); PanProbe 38/38 x2; Arkham Asylum (CPU-bound DXVK, quietd Stock, 10 interleaved rounds + 3) gameplay fps unchanged (median 36.4 base vs 36.55), launch failures 0/13 base vs 2/13 (known B5 signatures, Fisher p~0.48, n.s.); combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
